					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1161516#post-2262194</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-1161516/the-wolves-at-the-door#post-2262194</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 01 Apr 2015 17:11:39 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>SoullessSingularity</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>637830</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Eh, I don't like this tale as much. It's hardly a narrative as much as it is just a set-up scene- a stopover so to speak between narratives. Downvote.</p> <p>EDIT: I downvoted because I did not find interpersonal implications or imagery that were particularly insightful to me as a reader. I just couldn't really get into it and there was no moment that made me think &quot;huh, I never considered that&quot;.</p> <p>EDIT EDIT: This differs from other &quot;interlude esque&quot; pieces, such as TroyL's In His Own Image interludes, which provide enjoyable imagery/interpersonal investment to make intriguing snapshots between general narratives.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
